INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('195debe2-5690-4fc5-86eb-0a121e3fdde0','c5c04afb-db88-43d5-b192-2eba7d10458c','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user is asking which of the recently listed emails is the \"most urgent.\"\nUrgency is subjective and depends on context (e.g., Is it an alert? Does it require immediate action?).\nThe available tools do not have a concept of \"urgency.\"\nHowever, I can review the emails I presented and see if I can categorize them based on content (like \"action required,\" \"billing,\" \"security,\" \"security,\" etc.).\n\nThe previous results showed:\n1.  **Shop Weekly**: \"This week at the shop\" - Likely informational/promotional.\n2.  **Harness Bank**: \"INR 1,250.00 debited...\" - Financial/Action needed (verify/monitor).\n3.  **Raj Mehta**: \"Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8...\" - Calendar/Meeting (Scheduled for Oct 8th, which is in the future, not \"urgent\" in a crisis sense, but needs attention).\n4.  **Acme Store**: \"Your order A-42 has shipped** - Informational/Tracking.\n5.  **GitHub**: \"[GitHub] Your sign-in verification code\" - Security related (needs action/attention, but often time-sensitive).\n\nNone of these are inherently urgent in a breaking news sense.\nThe email from the bank or GitHub might require immediate verification/action depending on the user''s preference, but I cannot definitively label one as \"most urgent.\"\n\nI need to \"must\" try to provide a helpful answer.\nA good approach is to list the potential candidates and explain why I cannot definitively choose without more context, but I can point out the ones that typically warrant a closer look.\n\nSince I cannot *determine* urgency, I should present the options and ask the user for their priority, or state my limitations regarding urgency while highlighting the actionable items.\n\nWait, I should search my tools for any implicit \"urgency\" or \"priority\" markers.\nI will call `search_tools` just in case there is an implicit prioritization tool.\n\nTool search: `urgent` or `priority`.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user is asking which of the recently listed emails is the \"most urgent.\"\nUrgency is subjective and depends on context (e.g., Is it an alert? Does it require immediate action?).\nThe available tools do not have a concept of \"urgency.\"\nHowever, I can review the emails I presented and see if I can categorize them based on content (like \"action required,\" \"billing,\" \"security,\" \"security,\" etc.).\n\nThe previous results showed:\n1.  **Shop Weekly**: \"This week at the shop\" - Likely informational/promotional.\n2.  **Harness Bank**: \"INR 1,250.00 debited...\" - Financial/Action needed (verify/monitor).\n3.  **Raj Mehta**: \"Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8...\" - Calendar/Meeting (Scheduled for Oct 8th, which is in the future, not \"urgent\" in a crisis sense, but needs attention).\n4.  **Acme Store**: \"Your order A-42 has shipped** - Informational/Tracking.\n5.  **GitHub**: \"[GitHub] Your sign-in verification code\" - Security related (needs action/attention, but often time-sensitive).\n\nNone of these are inherently urgent in a breaking news sense.\nThe email from the bank or GitHub might require immediate verification/action depending on the user''s preference, but I cannot definitively label one as \"most urgent.\"\n\nI need to \"must\" try to provide a helpful answer.\nA good approach is to list the potential candidates and explain why I cannot definitively choose without more context, but I can point out the ones that typically warrant a closer look.\n\nSince I cannot *determine* urgency, I should present the options and ask the user for their priority, or state my limitations regarding urgency while highlighting the actionable items.\n\nWait, I should search my tools for any implicit \"urgency\" or \"priority\" markers.\nI will call `search_tools` just in case there is an implicit prioritization tool.\n\nTool search: `urgent` or `priority`."}],"createdAt":1793130833030},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"results":[{"name":"restoreEmail","description":"Restore an archived or trashed email in a specific mailbox back to the inbox.","score":3.42},{"name":"resumeWorkflowRun","description":"Retry the failed or blocked steps of one workflow run by the id listWorkflowRuns returned. Only a failed, partial or blocked run can be retried, wh...","score":3.4}],"loaded":["restoreEmail","resumeWorkflowRun"],"message":"Found and loaded 2 tool(s): restoreEmail, resumeWorkflowRun. They are available on your next turn — call them directly."},"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-be17d7703ef52ec7","toolName":"search_tools","args":{"query":"prioritize or urgent"}},"updatedAt":1793130833035},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1793130833039,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The tool search didn''t reveal any function specifically for judging email urgency. The loaded tools (`restoreEmail`, `resumeWorkflowRun`) are irrelevant to urgency.\n\nSince there is no tool to determine urgency, I must rely on the content and explain my assessment to the user.\n\nI will review the emails again and present a breakdown based on *action required* vs *informational*, while noting the temporal aspect.\n\n1.  **Harness Bank** (Financial): Needs monitoring/verification. High importance.\n2.  **GitHub** (Security): Needs awareness/action (did the user request this code?). High importance.\n3.  **Raj Mehta** (Calendar): Needs calendar acceptance/rejection (Future date). Medium importance.\n4.  **Acme Store** (Shipping): Informational. Low immediate importance.\n5.  **Shop Weekly** (Marketing): Informational. Low importance.\n\nI will frame the answer around these actionable categories instead of declaring a single \"most urgent\" email.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The tool search didn''t reveal any function specifically for judging email urgency. The loaded tools (`restoreEmail`, `resumeWorkflowRun`) are irrelevant to urgency.\n\nSince there is no tool to determine urgency, I must rely on the content and explain my assessment to the user.\n\nI will review the emails again and present a breakdown based on *action required* vs *informational*, while noting the temporal aspect.\n\n1.  **Harness Bank** (Financial): Needs monitoring/verification. High importance.\n2.  **GitHub** (Security): Needs awareness/action (did the user request this code?). High importance.\n3.  **Raj Mehta** (Calendar): Needs calendar acceptance/rejection (Future date). Medium importance.\n4.  **Acme Store** (Shipping): Informational. Low immediate importance.\n5.  **Shop Weekly** (Marketing): Informational. Low importance.\n\nI will frame the answer around these actionable categories instead of declaring a single \"most urgent\" email."}],"createdAt":1793130833068},{"type":"text","text":"Determining \"most urgent\" depends on your personal priorities, but based on the nature of the emails, here is a breakdown of which ones typically require the most immediate attention:\n\n*   **High Action Required (Security/Financial):**\n    *   **GitHub** — *\\[GitHub] Your sign-in verification code*: You should check if you initiated this sign-in attempt.\n    *   **Harness Bank** — *INR 1,250.00 debited from a/c \\*\\*4821*: Financial activity usually warrants immediate review.\n\n*   **Mid-Term Action Required (Planning):**\n    *   **Raj Mehta** — *Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8, 2026 15:00 UTC*: You should check your calendar to see if you need to accept or decline this meeting invitation.\n\n*   **Informational (Low Urgency):**\n    *   **Acme Store** — *Your order A-42 has shipped*: Tracking information.\n    *   **Shop Weekly** — *This week at the shop*: Marketing and promotions.\n\nIf you want me to look into any of these specific items (e.g., read the content of the bank email or check your calendar for the meeting), please let me know.","createdAt":1793130833068}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"Determining \"most urgent\" depends on your personal priorities, but based on the nature of the emails, here is a breakdown of which ones typically require the most immediate attention:\n\n*   **High Action Required (Security/Financial):**\n    *   **GitHub** — *\\[GitHub] Your sign-in verification code*: You should check if you initiated this sign-in attempt.\n    *   **Harness Bank** — *INR 1,250.00 debited from a/c \\*\\*4821*: Financial activity usually warrants immediate review.\n\n*   **Mid-Term Action Required (Planning):**\n    *   **Raj Mehta** — *Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8, 2026 15:00 UTC*: You should check your calendar to see if you need to accept or decline this meeting invitation.\n\n*   **Informational (Low Urgency):**\n    *   **Acme Store** — *Your order A-42 has shipped*: Tracking information.\n    *   **Shop Weekly** — *This week at the shop*: Marketing and promotions.\n\nIf you want me to look into any of these specific items (e.g., read the content of the bank email or check your calendar for the meeting), please let me know."}','assistant','v2','2026-10-27T19:53:53.030Z','7f765568-8c0d-56ce-8b89-105126fefedf');
