re.\"\n\nI will search for general terms that might indicate money leaving an account.\nNew keywords: \"deduction,\" \"cleared,\" \"refund,\" \"amount due,\" \"wire transfer,\" \"transfer sent,\" \"direct debit.\"\n\nI should also consider checking connected drives for financial folders or documents, although this is a long shot compared to email. Given the lack of results in email, I will broaden the email search first.\n\nI will execute the new search calls.The initial set of searches for common payment keywords (\"payment\", \"invoice\", \"billing charge\", \"transaction\", \"subscription\", \"bank withdrawal\") returned mostly empty or irrelevant results.\n\nHowever, the search for the general keyword \"payment\" returned 50 emails from \"Edge Sender\" in mailbox `ana@harness.test`. These emails are highly technical (e.g., \"html-hostile\", \"jsonld-1mb\", \"att-mislabeled-zip-as-pdf\") and do not look like personal financial transactions, but I must report what I find.\n\nI should check if the user meant \"money moving out\" in a more direct or personal sense. Since I''ve covered most common automated payment triggers, I will perform a broader search, including personal names or specific common services that might bill them, or look for \"statement\" or \"receipt\" which are strong indicators of money leaving an account.\n\nGiven the current results:\n1.  \"payment\": 50 irrelevant technical emails.\n2.  All others: 0 results.\n\nI will broaden the search to include \"statement\", \"receipt\", \"bank\", and \"debit\".\n\nI will run more parallel searches.\nKeywords: \"statement\", \"receipt\", \"debit\", \"bank\"\nI will continue to search across all mailboxes.All initial searches (payment, invoice, billing charge, transaction, subscription, bank withdrawal) returned either empty results or boilerplate/system emails (from \"Edge Sender\" - likely not financial transactions).\n\nHowever, the system returned 50 emails for the keyword \"payment\", but these were all internal, system-related emails about thread IDs and \"Long thread\" and not actual money moving.\n\nI need to broaden the search or check other relevant places.\nWhat about specific service payments? Or I could check the drive files for PDF invoices or statements.\n\nThe user asked \"Any money moving out of my accounts lately?\".\nSince I have covered the obvious email keywords, and found nothing conclusive, I should inform the user about the lack of immediate evidence in email and then check for financial documents in their connected drives.\n\nTool search: `search_tools` with keyword \"search files\" to load it.The user asked about any money moving out of their accounts lately.\nI have performed several searches across all mailboxes for keywords related to payments and financial transactions, including \"payment,\" \"invoice,\" \"billing charge,\" \"transaction,\" \"subscription,\" and \"bank withdrawal.\"\n\nAnalysis of Search Results:\n1.  `searchMail` for \"payment\": Returned 50 results, but all of them are highly suspicious and unrelated to actual financial payments. They are from \"Edge Sender\" and involve internal testing/coding subjects like \"html-hostile,\" \"jsonld-1mb,\" \"att-mislabeled-zip-as-pdf,\" etc. These appearThe user asks \"Any money moving out of my accounts lately?\"\n\nSearches for \"payment\", \"billing charge\", \"transaction\", \"subscription\", \"bank withdrawal\" all returned 0 results. The \"invoice\" search returned 50 results but they are all \"Edge Sender\" edge-case test emails (\"Re: Long thread\", \"jsonld-1mb\", \"att-hostile-filenames\", etc.) — irrelevant noise. So no billing/payment emails in the mailbox.\n\nHmm, but wait. \"money moving out of my accounts\" — could there be bank/account info elsewhere? Maybe drive files? Or maybe the \"Acme Store\" order A-42 is a purchase (money out). But the question asks \"lately\" — order A-42 shipped Sep 23; the order was placed earlier.\n\nLet me consider searching drives for financial statements. But is there a drive tool loaded? I don''t have searchFiles loaded. Actually, in earlier turns I used listDrives and searchFiles? Looking back at the conversation, I see listDrives was called. But the tools currently listed in my function list are only the base ones plus what''s been loaded: addReadLater, aggregateInbox, createEvent, findMemberEvents, getEmail, listCalendars, listDrives, listEvents, listMailboxes, listMuted, listReadLater, markRead, removeReadLater, searchMail, search_tools. So no searchFiles currently loaded. But the user''s question is about \"money moving out of my accounts\" — probably a mail-based question (bank alerts, payment notifications). My searches found nothing relevant.\n\nLet me broaden: search for \"paid\", \"charged\", \"receipt\", \"statement\", \"wire\", \"transfer\", \"Stripe\", \"PayPal\", \"refund\", \"debit\". Also maybe aggregateInbox to see recent inbox activity across mailboxes — but only one mailbox appears to exist (ana@harness.test). Actually, let me check listMailboxes — earlier turns used it? In this conversation''s visible history, listMailboxes wasn''t called explicitly in my visible turns. The prompt says to call listMailboxes when I need a mailboxId I can''t name. searchMail across all mailboxes returned only ana@harness.test results. So there may be multiple mailboxes; the search covered all.\n\nLet me run a second round of searches: \"charged\", \"receipt\", \"bank statement\", \"wire transfer\", \"debited\", \"money\", \"paid\", \"refund\".\n\nAlso, maybe check drives for financial docs — but first mail. Let me do parallel searches.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The initial searches for financial keywords (\"payment\", \"invoice\", \"billing charge\", \"transaction\", \"subscription\", \"bank withdrawal\") across all mailboxes returned mostly empty results, with one set of emails from \"Edge Sender\" which are clearly technical/system noise and irrelevant.\n\nSince the standard financial