ages.* The last search revealed 34 unread emails. Furthermore, even after reading many pages of \"test\" Re: Long thread\" noise, there are several structurally unusual unread emails (date-missing, date-garbage, etc.).\n2.  **Prioritized To-Do List Generation:**\n    *   **Calendar Events:**\n        *   *Daily Standup (Work Calendar):* Remaining this week (Wed Oct 28, Thu Oct 29, Fri Oct 30) at 09:00 UTC.\n        *   *Bulk/Testing Deadlines (Sunday Oct 31):* 12 synthetic deadline/invoice/contract events. (Note: These are likely test data test imports, I must phrase this cautiously).\n        *   *Other Fixed Dates:* Oct 31 drafts for \"Bulk 168\" and \"Bulk 0\".\n    *   **Actionable Emails (Mail):**\n        *   *Real-world:* Acme Store shipment, GitHub codeNow I have all ~284 inbox emails. The inbox is overwhelmingly a test/edge-case fixture: \"Re: Long thread\" (~200 emails from Edge Sender), mime edge cases, date edge cases. Only real-ish emails from page 1: Rebrand review invitation (Oct 8), Rebrand kickoff (Sep 21), Acme Store shipment, bank debit, GitHub code, Shop Weekly newsletter.\n\nAll of these are READ except... let me check: first page (284 down to 235) — all isRead true. Second page (234 down to 185) — all isRead false. Third page — false. Fourth — false. Fifth — false. So unread count ≈ 234 down to 1 → 234 emails unread? Wait, first page covered IDs 284..235 (50 items, all read). Second page 234..185 all unread. Third 184..135 unread. Fourth 134..85 unread. Fifth 84..35 unread. Sixth 34..1 (34 items) unread. So unread = 234 emails. Hmm, but that includes the \"Re: Long thread\" 200-message thread (IDs ~186-235 down to ...) and the edge-case mime ones. So unread ≈ 234, but almost entirely fixture noise.\n\nWait — careful. Page 5 results showed IDs 42, 44, 38, 84, 83 ... down to 45, 40, 39, 41, 43, plus mime-nested etc. And page 6 IDs 34 down to 1. So total 284 emails in inbox, 50 read (the top 50), 234 unread. But those \"unread\" are largely the long-thread noise.\n\nI should present the to-do list honestly: the signal here is thin. Real actionable items:\n1. **Rebrand kickoff** — Raj Mehta''s kickoff thread (Sep 21) plus the \"Rebrand review\" meeting invitation for Thu Oct 8 (already passed, 19 days ago) — and the rebrand folder brief.txt exists in 4 drives. Action: the rebrand review never happened / reschedule, or confirm whether rebrand is done. Also drives all contain `rebrand/brief.txt` — a deliverable to review.\n2. **Bulk calendar deadlines Sun 1 Nov** — 12 events all \"deadline\"/\"invoice\"/\"package\"/\"contract\" at 00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00, 20:00 on Nov 1. These look bulk-imported/synthetic; verify whether real. If real, they''re the only hard deadlines this week — but they''re all on Sunday.\n3. **Acme Store shipment** — order #4821 shipped Sep 28 — check delivery this week.\n4. **Bank debit** — R$59.90 debited Sep 28 — reconcile.\n5. **GitHub code** — verification code 841205 from Sep 28 — expired, ignore; but if a sign-in is pending, re-request.\n6. **Inbox triage** — 234 unread, ~200 from one \"Re: Long thread\" thread → mute/archive; plus ~40 edge-case/MIME test messages and impossible dates (year 9999, epoch 1970, \"sometime next tuesday-ish\") — these look like test fixtures in the production inbox, worth cleaning up or flagging to whoever runs the harness.\n7. **Newsletter** — Shop Weekly \"This week at the shop\" (Sep 26) — only newsletter/digest found; read-later candidate, no action.\n8. **Daily standup** — Work calendar, 09:00 UTC weekdays; remaining this week Wed 28 – Fri 30 Oct. Today''s already past (12:40 UTC).\n9. **Calendar hygiene** — \"Daily forever\" duplicate in Edge cases calendar mirroring standup times; \"Ten year all-day event\" spanning 2026-2036 blocking whole decade — should be deleted or scoped.\n10. **Drive scoping** — FTP 7966bf69 only exposes rebrand/, so the \"same files everywhere\" question can''t be fully answered; also two S3 drives have extra edge/